  <div class=\"sub-logo\">中国日报</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"url\">| www.chinadaily.com.cn</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <table class=\"table-container\">\n        <tr>\n            <td class=\"table-col-1\">\n                began to get a little less dark in 1477, when Archduke Maximilian of Austria <span class=\"highlight-red\">commissioned[5]</span> an extravagant diamond ring for his new wife. The <span class=\"highlight-red\">accessory[6]</span> grew in popularity in the Victorian era, and gradually the diamond ring trend <span class=\"highlight-red\">trickled down[7]</span> from nobility to the masses.\n            </td>\n            <td class=\"table-col-2\">\n                米兰至公给新婚妻子定制了一枚奢侈的钻石戒指，自那以后订婚戒指的含义就没那么阴暗了。订婚戒指在维多利亚时代变得越发流行，订婚钻戒的习俗也从贵族流传到了民间。\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n    </table>\n\n    <div class=\"vocabulary-list\">\n        <div class=\"vocab-item\">\n            <span class=\"vocab-number\">[1]</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-word\">twisted</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-pronunciation\">美 /'twɪstɪd/</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-def\"><span class=\"vocab-type\">adj.</span> mentally or emotionally unsound or disturbed <span class=\"vocab-def-cn\">扭曲的</span></span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-example\">She gave a small twisted smile. <span class=\"vocab-example-cn\">她不不自然地微微一笑。</span></span>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"vocab-item\">\n            <span class=\"vocab-number\">[2]</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-word\">gem</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-pronunciation\">美 /dʒem/</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-def\"><span class=\"vocab-type\">n.</span> (also gemstone) a precious stone that has been cut and polished and is used in jewellery <span class=\"vocab-def-cn\">（经切割打磨的）宝石</span></span>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"vocab-item\">\n            <span class=\"vocab-number\">[3]</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-word\">anthropologist</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-pronunciation\">美 /ˌænθrə'pɑːlədʒɪst/</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-def vocab-inline\"><span class=\"vocab-type\">n.</span> <span class=\"vocab-def-cn\">人类学家</span></span>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"vocab-item\">\n            <span class=\"vocab-number\">[4]</span>\n            <span class=\"highlight-bg\">\n                <span class=\"vocab-word\">date back to... /date from...</span>\n                <span class=\"vocab-def-cn\">追溯到；始于；自…至今</span>\n            </span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-example\">The college dates back to medieval times.<br><span class=\"vocab-example-cn\">这所学院创办于中世纪。</span></span>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"vocab-item\">\n            <span class=\"vocab-number\">[5]</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-word highlight-bg-yellow\">commission</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-def-cn highlight-bg-yellow\">熟词僻义</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-def highlight-bg-yellow\" style=\"margin-left: 0; margin-top: 10px; display: inline-block;\"><span class=\"vocab-type\">v.</span> to officially ask sb to write, make or create sth or to do a task for you <span class=\"vocab-def-cn\">正式委托（谱写或制作、创作、完成）</span></span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-example\" style=\"margin-left: 0;\">Publishers have commissioned a French translation of the book.<br><span class=\"vocab-example-cn\">出版商已委托人把这本书译成法语。</span></span>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"vocab-item\">\n            <span class=\"vocab-number\">[6]</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-word\">accessory</span>\n            <span class=\"vocab-pronunciation\">美 /ək'sesəri/</span>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n</body>\n</html>"
